{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Canonical diagrams of Boolean functions and families of sets."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"DecisionDiagrams"}],"role":"collection","title":"DecisionDiagrams","externalID":"DecisionDiagrams","symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"},{"text":" is a table of reduced ordered binary decision diagrams (Bryant,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1986). Each function is a directed acyclic graph whose vertices test variables in index order,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a low child for the variable false and a high child for true, down to the constants. No two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices test the same variable with the same children, and none has equal children, so each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"function has exactly one root, and checking whether two functions are equal is comparing roots.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import DecisionDiagrams","","var diagram = BinaryDecisionDiagram(variableCount: 3)","let x0 = diagram.variable(0), x1 = diagram.variable(1), x2 = diagram.variable(2)","let f = diagram.or(diagram.and(x0, x1), x2)   \/\/ x0 ∧ x1 ∨ x2","diagram.satisfyingAssignmentCount(of: f)       \/\/ 5","diagram.anySatisfyingAssignment(of: f)         \/\/ [false, false, true]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The diagram of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" has five vertices: three tests and the two constants. Following the low edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"means the variable is false, the high edge that it is true."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Tests","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Low child"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"High child"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"root"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"the test of ","type":"text"},{"code":"x2","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x1"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"the test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"true"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"false","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"true","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The test of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"type":"text","text":" is shared: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0"},{"type":"text","text":" false and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x0 ∧ ¬x1"},{"type":"text","text":" both leave "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"f"},{"type":"text","text":" equal to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x2"},{"type":"text","text":", so both lead"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the one vertex that stands for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Functions combine under any of the sixteen binary operators with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/apply(_:_:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" in O(|"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"f","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"| |"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"g"}]},{"type":"text","text":"|), through a computed table of results"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already found. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/restrict(_:variable:to:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" fixes a variable, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/exists(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/forall(_:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" quantify"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over variables. The table’s vertices are a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so Grafluent’s traversals and drawings run over a function’s diagram from its root."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"},{"text":" is a table of families of sets (Minato, 1993). Its vertices","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test elements in index order, with a low child for the sets without the element and a high child","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for those with it. In place of the rule that removes a vertex with equal children, it removes one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose high child is the empty family, so an element no set contains never appears in a diagram,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a sparse family over many elements stays small.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var diagram = ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram(elementCount: 3)","let f = diagram.family([[0, 1], [1, 2], [2]])","diagram.count(of: f)                                 \/\/ 3","diagram.minimalSets(of: diagram.including(2, in: f)) \/\/ {{2}}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Families combine by "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/union(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/intersection(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/subtracting(_:from:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", and set by set by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/join(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/meet(_:_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/setsView(of:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" lists a family’s sets, and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" like the binary diagram’s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Binary-decision-diagrams","title":"Binary decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram"]},{"anchor":"Zero-suppressed-decision-diagrams","title":"Zero-suppressed decision diagrams","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/ZeroSuppressedDecisionDiagram"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://DecisionDiagrams/documentation/DecisionDiagrams/BinaryDecisionDiagram/Function/vertex":{"title":"vertex","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/Function\/vertex","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The function’s root, as a vertex of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/DecisionDiagrams\/documentation\/DecisionDiagrams\/BinaryDecisionDiagram\/graphView-swift.property","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": 0 for false, 1","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for true.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams\/binarydecisiondiagram\/function\/vertex"},"doc://DecisionDiagrams/documentati